<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Tarkhan dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1554 CE – 1591 CE · capital Thatta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Mongol-descended dynasty that ruled lower Sindh from Thatta between the Arghuns and the Mughal conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirza-isa-tarkhan">Mirza Isa Tarkhan</a>, an officer of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arghun-dynasty">Arghun dynasty</a> descended from a Mongol military family, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thatta">Thatta</a> in 1554 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arghun">Arghun</a> authority collapsed. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-husain-arghun">Shah Husain Arghun's</a> death he became master of lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, ruling from Thatta in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> delta.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Tarkhans ruled a prosperous delta region with the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahari-bandar">Lahari Bandar</a>, trading with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> and the Portuguese. The Portuguese sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thatta">Thatta</a> in 1555 after a dispute. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirza-isa-tarkhan">Mirza Isa</a> and his successors built tombs at the Makli necropolis, adding Persian-style monuments to the earlier Samma tombs.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirza-jani-beg-tarkhan">Mirza Jani Beg Tarkhan</a> was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar's</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-rahim-khan-i-khanan">Abdul Rahim Khan-i-Khanan</a> and submitted in 1591. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, though Tarkhan descendants served as governors for a time.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tarkhan-dynasty.jpg" alt="Tarkhan dynasty" width="320" height="152"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tarkhans._temp._Mirza_Muhammad_Baqi_Tarkhan._AH_975-993_AD_1567-1585_Tatta_mint._Dated_AH_985_(1577-8).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1554 CE – 1591 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thatta</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mirza Isa Tarkhan, Mirza Jani Beg Tarkhan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, Sindhi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tarkhans of Sindh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1572&amp;focus=tarkhan-dynasty" aria-label="Tarkhan dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6483 1267 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tarkhan dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6803 1523L6832 1282M6803 1523L7018 1385"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6832 1282h0M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6803 1523h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6803 1523h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thatta. <a href="/atlas?year=1572&amp;focus=tarkhan-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
